Entries above 2.0 are outside the band the coefficients were
fitted on. That is a reason a coarse grid can be bad on the
rotated scheme; it is not a reason a FINE one can be worse,
because every argument falls as h falls.

SCALE. A 1 per cent phase-velocity error moves the 16 mm arrival
by 0.040 us, which is 8 per cent of the +-0.5 us echo gate.

DISPERSION-ONLY AMPLITUDE. A Ricker at F0 is propagated 2d = 16.0 mm
through each scheme by giving every frequency its own numerical
phase velocity, with NO geometric spreading and NO attenuation.
The envelope peak that survives is what pulse spreading alone
costs, so it bounds how much of the measured tilt swing can be
dispersion rather than source directivity.
